{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/BiconnectedComponents","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/BlockCutTree","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Condensation","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/DominanceFrontiers","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/DominatorTree","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/KComponents"],"title":"Structures","generated":true},{"anchor":"Extended-Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Trees"],"title":"Extended Modules","generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Connectivity"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"Connectivity","externalID":"Connectivity","symbolKind":"module"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/Trees":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Trees","type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/trees","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","title":"Trees"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/BiconnectedComponents":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The biconnected components (blocks) of an undirected graph: a collection of blocks, each the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions of its edges in ascending order; blocks are ordered by their smallest edge position."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The blocks partition the edges that are not self-loops."}],"title":"BiconnectedComponents","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/biconnectedcomponents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/BiconnectedComponents","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BiconnectedComponents"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BiconnectedComponents"}]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/KComponents":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-components of an undirected graph (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k ≥ 1,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the maximal sets of vertices whose induced subgraph is k-vertex-connected, that is, has more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than k vertices and stays connected after removing any k − 1 of them. The 1-components are the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connected components with an edge, the 2-components the blocks of three or more vertices; every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"k-component lies inside a (k − 1)-component. Components at one level may share fewer than k"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices."}],"title":"KComponents","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/kcomponents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/KComponents","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KComponents"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"KComponents"}]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","title":"Connectivity","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity","type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/DominanceFrontiers":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/DominanceFrontiers","type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/dominancefrontiers","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DominanceFrontiers","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The dominance frontier of each vertex reachable from a root: the vertices ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"y"},{"text":" such that the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex dominates a predecessor of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"y"},{"type":"text","text":" but does not strictly dominate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"y"},{"type":"text","text":" (Cytron et al.), where"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SSA construction places φ-functions."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"DominanceFrontiers","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DominanceFrontiers"}]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/BlockCutTree":{"title":"BlockCutTree","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/BlockCutTree","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/blockcuttree","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The block–cut tree of an undirected graph (Harary’s block-cutpoint tree): a node per block and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per articulation point, and an edge joining each block to each articulation point it contains."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Blocks are numbered as in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"blocks"},{"type":"text","text":", articulation points by their place in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"articulationPoints"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order). It is a forest: one tree per connected component with an edge that is not a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop; isolated vertices are no node."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BlockCutTree"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BlockCutTree"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols":{"abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/DominatorTree":{"kind":"symbol","title":"DominatorTree","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DominatorTree","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/DominatorTree","abstract":[{"text":"The dominator tree of the vertices reachable from a root: ","type":"text"},{"code":"a","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" dominates ","type":"text"},{"code":"b","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when every path","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the root to ","type":"text"},{"code":"b","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" passes through ","type":"text"},{"code":"a","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each reachable vertex but the root has an immediate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dominator, its closest strict dominator, which is its parent in the tree.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/dominatortree","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DominatorTree","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/Condensation":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Condensation","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Condensation","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Condensation","abstract":[{"text":"A graph’s strongly connected components and the acyclic graph between them.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/condensation","role":"symbol","naviga